* L55 COPIA DI BANCO di models/bjt_pnp/mje253.lib: modello rinominato Qmje253F, e in fondo le capacita' di
* giunzione ferme a TNOM (script/modelli_banco.py). NON e' un modello del progetto.
* mje253.lib - onsemi MJE253G, PNP complementary silicon power plastic
* transistor, TO-225, 100 V / 4.0 A / 15 W (TC = 25 C).
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_pnp/mje253.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter Qmje253
*
* NOTE THE MODEL NAME: it is Qmje253, not MJE253. The vendor named it that
* way and it was not "corrected".
*
* Role in this project: NC-056 (L55). CANDIDATE driver-sized replacement
* for the MJE15033 in the Class A emitter follower of the gain block
* (circuits/preamp/gain_block.py:717-718). NOT YET USED BY ANY CIRCUIT: see
* models/bjt_npn/mje243.lib.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_pnp/mje253.provenance.json, the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_pnp/onsemi/MJE253/PROVENANCE.json, and the sourcing and
* measurements in docs/preamp/data/2026-10-29/L55/modelli/README.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* onsemi serves this model at /download/models/lib/mje253.lib (200,
* application/octet-stream, 996 bytes). The header was read before
* freezing (limitations #20): '.MODEL Qmje253 pnp' - the right part. Frozen
* byte-for-byte at vendor/bjt_pnp/onsemi/MJE253/mje253.lib and copied here
* unchanged.
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_pnp/onsemi/MJE253/mje253.lib) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_pnp/mje253.lib)   # the KF/AF line only
*
* THE MODEL WAS WRITTEN BY A CONTRACTOR (MODPEX / Symmetry Design Systems,
* "Model generated on Jan 22, 03", PSpice format) and onsemi distributes it.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET - INSIDE EVERY WINDOW
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Datasheet MJE243/D Rev. 17 (the same document, vendor/bjt_npn/onsemi/
* MJE243/mje243-d.pdf). ngspice 47, set temp = 25, |VCE| as the datasheet:
*
*   hFE @ IC = 200 mA, VCE = 1 V      45.106    40 MIN / 180 MAX  inside
*   hFE @ IC = 1.0 A,  VCE = 1 V      23.658    15 MIN            inside
*   fT  @ IC = 100 mA, VCE = 10 V,
*       ftest = 10 MHz                59.896 MHz  40 MHz MIN      inside
*   Cob @ VCB = 10 V, IE = 0, 0.1 MHz 19.695 pF   50 pF MAX        inside
*       (datasheet Fig. 7, typical at 10 V: ~17 pF)
*
* The hFE at 200 mA is only 12.8 % above the 40 minimum: this model is a
* low-gain PNP (BF = 54). Recipe: tb_mje253() in scripts/validate_models.py.
*
* AT THE FOLLOWER'S OWN POINT (20 mA, VCE 15 V): hFE 209, Vbe 0.626 V,
* gm 761 mS, Cpi 2.19 nF, Cmu 14.6 pF, fT 61 MHz (unity crossing). The
* MJE15033 under the same script: hFE 237, Vbe 0.543 V, Cpi 7.81 nF,
* Cmu 64 pF, fT 12 MHz.
* THE MODEL'S VJC IS 0.0329 V (a vendor parameter, left as served): the
* collector-base capacitance falls much faster with reverse bias than a
* usual junction. It reproduces the datasheet (Cob 19.7 pF against ~17 pF in
* Fig. 7) at 10 V; below ~1 V it should not be trusted.
*
* NO FLICKER NOISE FROM THE MANUFACTURER (KF=0 AF=1 in the vendor card);
* the ADR-057 bound is appended at the end of this file.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE VENDOR FILE FOLLOWS, BYTE FOR BYTE (CRLF line endings, mixed on
* purpose, limitations #39).
